config BR2_PACKAGE_HC800_ACPI
	bool "hc800-acpi (ACPI table upgrade: the IO microcontroller)"
	depends on BR2_i386 || BR2_x86_64
	help
	  Compiles the HC-800's own ACPI tables (board/hc800/acpi/*.asl)
	  with the host iasl and packs them as an uncompressed cpio under
	  kernel/firmware/acpi/, which post-image.sh puts in front of the
	  initrd. The kernel loads them early as an ACPI table upgrade
	  (CONFIG_ACPI_TABLE_UPGRADE).

	  Today that is one SSDT: the LM3S1162 IO microcontroller as a
	  serdev child of the BIOS's ttyS3, so gpio-ohc-iomcu binds it at
	  boot with no userspace attach.
